# KNOWN_BEHIND: the rows of the gate where lengua is behind by more than the gate's noise margin
# (todo.md's finish line, point 4; src/gate.rs reads this file). A row is a runner, a workload, the
# version lengua is set against, and a measure, each a name or * for every one, and what follows a
# # says why:
#
# - runners: linux-x86_64, linux-aarch64, macos-aarch64, windows-x86_64, windows-aarch64;
# - workloads: empty, add, hypotenuse, upcase, upcase-stdin, shout, wc, histogram, crc32c, sort,
#   tally, server, files, readings;
# - versions: c-wasm, cpp-wasm and rust-wasm, compiled to WebAssembly and run the same way as
#   lengua's program; c, cpp and rust, built natively with the runner's own compilers;
# - measures: cpu, wall, memory, size.
#
# The margin is 5% (MARGIN in src/gate.rs; the owner's decision of 2026-11-11). A measure is level
# when the test doesn't decide it, or when lengua's value is from 0.95 to 1.05 times the other
# version's; size has no margin. A level row has no line here and fails no run.
#
# The list may only shrink. `cargo bench --bench against_rust_and_c` fails on a runner when it finds
# lengua behind by more than the margin on a row the list doesn't name, or level or ahead on a row
# it names, and it writes target/bench/KNOWN_BEHIND-<runner>.txt, the rows that would pass, into the
# run's artifacts. A row the run couldn't measure keeps the line it has. The bench also fails when
# a change to this file, anywhere in the history it measures, named a row the list before the
# change didn't: lines may be taken out or made narrower, never added or widened, except for a
# runner, a workload, a version or a measure the gate didn't have before.
#
# Each runner's lines below began as the rows where lengua wasn't ahead in its first gate run
# (https://github.com/laughing-hermit/lengua/actions/runs/42661776298, at 9a549b3), which took
# the place of a line naming every row of the runner, less those where it was ahead in a later
# run: https://github.com/laughing-hermit/lengua/actions/runs/42728160641 (at d6496e3, lengua's
# run made lean, W12b), https://github.com/laughing-hermit/lengua/actions/runs/42756074550 (at
# 076bcc1, faster programs, W12c) and
# https://github.com/laughing-hermit/lengua/actions/runs/42947294489 (at 33ed7fe, the finish-line
# run, W15), which left 1,037. The first run with the margin,
# https://github.com/laughing-hermit/lengua/actions/runs/42964232679 (at cd54e79), found 139 of
# them level or ahead, and they left: 898 rows stay, each one behind by more than the margin in
# that run. That run also found 6 rows behind by more than the margin that the list doesn't name,
# as it may not grow: todo.md lists them under "A row the gate can't decide".
# The first run with lengua-run (W19), https://github.com/laughing-hermit/lengua/actions/runs/43084459708
# (at 45b507b; Windows on ARM64 again in 43099764273, whose first report was lost with its upload),
# found 135 more level and 2 ahead, and they left: 761 rows stay. It found 26 rows behind by more
# than the margin that the list doesn't name, 4 of the 6 among them; todo.md lists them.
# The first run where the other modules make lengua's checks (decided 2026-11-11),
# https://github.com/laughing-hermit/lengua/actions/runs/43131768685 (at 43813ae; macOS on ARM64
# in 43145761976, as the first's runner lost its connection), found 25 more level, and they
# left: 736 rows stay. It found 10 rows behind by more than the margin that the list doesn't
# name, 4 of the 26 among them; todo.md lists them.

